          "ordinal": 1,
          "status": "submitted",
          "responses": {
            "assessment_item_cf49e645-9e25-47f9-b6ec-f91fc7b2b964": "(1) Y is heavier than X. (Since 7kg > 4kg, the comparative form heavier than correctly compares the two stones.)\n(2) Z is the heaviest of the three stones. (Since 10kg is the largest among 4kg, 7kg, 10kg, the superlative requires 'the' and the explicit range 'of the three stones'.)\n(3) Key difference: The comparative is for exactly two objects and normally uses 'than' to connect the second object (e.g., A is heavier than B). The superlative is for one object within a given set of three or more, and must use 'the' with an explicit range such as 'of the three' to indicate the comparison set; it does not pair with a single other object via 'than'."
          },
          "startedAt": "2026-09-14T12:00:45.896Z",
          "submittedAt": "2026-09-14T12:01:25.648Z",
